  "rationale": "The clause supports blocking a projected balance above the sanctioned limit when explicit consent is absent. However, the frozen source contains an orphan OR and END-IF, so it does not establish executable prior acceptance or rejection behavior. The validator itself correctly flags overlimit balances; the proposed contradictory gate interpretation is plausible but not demonstrated by a complete conditional. The packet needs to distinguish syntax restoration, inferred gate behavior, and regulatory remediation before treating this as a D3 contradictory case with preserved regressions.",
  "scope_judgment": "The allowlisted lines contain the orphan gate and validator branch bodies, allowing a local repair consistent with the finite no-consent fixtures. They do not contain a consent input or establish an explicit-consent pathway. Scope is defensible for conservative overlimit blocking, but does not support a full compliance claim or an independently established original gate.",
  "intended_fixture_judgment": "The 100-limit, 200-projected-balance fixture has a clause-grounded expected result of POSTED: N under the stated no-consent assumption. It is a proposed expectation, not an executed pass. Equality and zero-limit coverage are present elsewhere, but coverage should also include the smallest representable excess above the limit and fractional balances to exercise the declared cent precision. No consent-present behavior is modeled or tested.",
